{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792552734230,"sessionID":"ses_ea38a7238ffepix1NRgG7ZnjW2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"websearch","callID":"call_9b211645b6b747eea5d8388f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"query":"Capsida Biotherapeutics NR001 NR005 pipeline capsid","numResults":8},"output":"Title: Identification of Multiple Novel Blood-Brain Barrier Receptors for CNS Gene Therapy and Other Drug Modalities via an Integrated AAV Capsid Engineering Platform\nURL: https://capsida.com/wp-content/uploads/Nick_Goeden_1445_May-14_Theater-C_Identification-of-Multiple-BBB-Receptors.pdf\nPublished: 2025-05-14T00:00:00.000Z\nAuthor: Mansi Dave\nHighlights:\nof Multiple Novel Blood-Brain Barrier Receptors for CNS Gene Therapy and Other Drug Modalities via an Integrated AAV Capsid Engineering Platform\n\n...\n\nThis presentation ... information regarding ... research and ... programs of Capsida ... other ... , Inc ... that are based on or derived from preclinical data. Clinical trial results may differ. Capsida does not ... an approved therapy presently available for STXBP1 Developmental and Epileptic ... cephalopathy, Parkinson ... s disease associated with GBA mutations ... or Friedreich's ataxia, ... there any promise ... guarantee that Capsida's research and development will produce any potential ... in ... future.\n\n...\n\nCapsida is the first genetic medicines company with FDA IND clearance for an engineered IV-delivered gene therapy that crosses the blood-brain-barrier and detargets liver\n\n...\n\n1Abstract #123; Wednesday, 3:45-4:00p in NOLA Theater B presented by Nicholas Flytzanis, Ph.D. \n2Abstract #1435, Wednesday Poster Session, presented by Kim McDowell, Ph.D. \n3Abstract #75, Wednesday, 1:45-2 pm, presented by Celeste Stephany, Ph.D. \n\nCAP-002: STXBP1-DEE1\n\nIND clearance ODD granted\n\nExternal Validation\n\nStrategic partnerships\n\nContract manufacturing\n\n1st AbbVie opt-in achieved\n\nFully-integrated Capabilities » Capsid engineering » Cargo optimization » Clinical development » In-house GMP manufacturing » Protected by expansive IP portfolio\n\nWholly-owned Pipeline\n\nCAP-004: Friedreich’s ataxia3\n\nCAP-003: PD-GBA2 • Human POC in Q4\n\nTwo clinical programs in 2025\n\nThird clinical program in 2026\n\n...\n\n#### Capsida is Uniquely Positioned to Lead Gene Therapy\n\nCapsid Engineering Scale CNS Tropism >99% specific to neurons at the capsid level >70% neurons transduced Broad IP portfolio protecting capsids and capsid/cargo\n\nPeripheral De-targeting\n\n>16x liver detargeted and >50x \nDRG detargeting \nSuperior off-target safety profile \nBroad IP portfolio protecting de \ntargeting \n\nSafe Therapeutic Expression Clinical Translatability\n\nIdentified and patented novel human receptor with complete homology in NHPs and humans Validated expression in NHPs including primates >20 years old\n\n...\n\nand GMP ... Productivity surpassing ... 9 Quality ... FDA\n\n...\n\nCapsida Has Built a Field-leading Capsid Engineering Platform High-throughput Automated Process Identifies Multiple Capsid Families with Efficient CNS Targeting\n\nEvolving Capsids to Meet Target Capsid Profile Iterative Screenings Yield Multiple High-performing Capsids\n\nMultiple Capsid Families\n\nNeuron-Specific Screening Construct\n\nMultiple independent screens have identified >5 distinct novel capsids with breakthrough CNS performance\n\n...\n\n#### Capsida’s Platform Delivers Multiple Novel Capsids that Exceed Target Capsid Profiles for CNS\n\n#### Lead Capsid Transduces Majority of Neurons Throughout the\n\n#### CNS Across 3 Wholly-Owned Programs at Low E13 vg/kg Dose\n\nCortex: Genetic Epilepsy\n\nHA-GOI NeuN\n\n500µm\n\nDeep brain structures: Parkinson’s Disease\n\n2 mm\n\n500µm\n\nN ig r a\n\nHA-GOI NeuN HA-GOI TH\n\nMotor neurons and deep cerebellar nuclei: Friedreich’s Ataxia\n\nHA-GOI CALBINDIN\n\n100 µm\n\nHA-GOI SMI32\n\n200 µm\n\nC o r d\n\nHA-GOI SMI32\n\n100 µm\n\n...\n\n### Lead Capsids Enable Robust Therapeutic Expression\n\nCAP-003 CAP004\n\nTherapeutic expression levels exceed clinically relevant thresholds – IND Clearance of CAP-002 provides the strongest validation of lead capsid’s therapeutic potential\n\nGCase Protein Expression Frataxin Protein Expression\n\n...\n\n#### Neuronal-Specific Transduction Enables Safer and More Effective CNS Gene Therapies\n\nNeuron-specific transduction across 3 wholly-owned programs improves safety and efficacy\n\n500µm 50µm\n\nCapsida’s lead CNS capsid achieved high neuronal specificity, minimizing off-target transduction and improving the safety profile of CNS-targeted gene therapies.\n\n• 99% neuronal specificity across the CNS \n• Specificity achieved via cell type-specific selection pressure \n• Minimized off-target cell transduction reduces toxicity risk \n• Achieved efficient, cell-type-targeted delivery across 3 programs \n\nHA-GOI NeuN\n\n...\n\n#### Reduced Off-target Biodistribution Improves Safety Profile\n\nCAP-002 CAP-003 CAP-004\n\n• All three programs show peripheral detargeting from key off-target tissues (liver and DRG) of first-generation gene therapies using wild-type AAV \n• No adverse clinical pathology or histopathological findings throughout the CNS, DRGs, or peripheral organs (including the liver) at all doses tested \n\nLiver DNA DRG RNA Liver DNA DRG RNA Liver DNA DRG RNA\n\n* Historical IV-delivered AAV9 2.5E13 vg/kg (tool cargo); 4 weeks expression\n\n...\n\n### Capsida’s Lead Capsid Has Favorable Manufacturability,\n\n### Well Positioned for Clinical Success\n\n| | | Manufacturability | | Scalability |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| | | | | |\n| | Characteristic | Industry Standard AAV9 | Capsida Lead Capsid | |\n| | Productivity in crude lysate | 1E11 vg/ml | 6.2E11 vg/ml | |\n| | Packaging (Empty/Full) | >70% | ~90% | |\n| | Aggregation | < 10% | 5% | |\n| | Overall Recovery | ~25% | 36% | |\n| | Capsida’s yield, improved purity, and greater recovery, overcoming key manufacturability hurdles for engineered AAVs | lead capsid outperforms AAV9 with higher | | |\n\n...\n\nIn-house PD and GMP manufacturing capabilities enable seamless scale-up from preclinical to commercial supply\n\nClinical supply for CAP-002 and CAP-003 has been produced and released Clinical trial start-up activities have initiated for CAP-002\n\n##### Identification of Distinct Novel Receptors with High Cross-Species Conservation Significantly De-Risks Clinical Translatability\n\nNR001 NR002 NR003 NR004 NR005\n\nNovel Capsid A\n\nNovel Capsid B\n\nNovel Capsid C\n\nNovel Capsid D\n\nNovel Capsid E\n\nNHP 96% 99% 96% 98% 93%\n\nSequence Identity to Human\n\n*Sequence identity is calculated across full protein and is not restricted to predicted binding site\n\nCapsida Biotherapeutics has successfully filed patents for all five of these groundbreaking novel receptors and is focused on further expanding the IP portfolio surrounding them\n\nThe predictive power of in vitro receptor binding is confirmed by AAV transduction in cell lines with receptor expression\n\nBinding also confirmed for NR002-5\n\nPlate-Based Receptor Binding Detection Bead-Based Receptor Binding Detection\n\nHuman and NHP ortholog binding confirmed\n\n##### In Vitro Binding Platform Demonstrates Reproducible Capsid/Receptor Binding Data Consistent with Expression Profiles\n\n#### Novel Receptors Highly Expressed in Neurons and Brain Endothelial Cells Enable More Specific Delivery to the CNS\n\n• Improved safety profile \n• Lower expression in off-target cell types relative to TfR \n• Differentiated CNS delivery mechanisms \n• NR004: endothelial-specific \n• NR002: broad expression across CNS cell types, enabling intracellular delivery \n• Broad IP protection \n\nReceptor RNA Expression in Human\n\nIntravitreal (IVT) Injections in Ocular Tissue Suprachoroidal (SCS) Injections in Ocular Tissue\n\n...\n\n#### Engineered Ocular Capsids Poised to Be Best-in-Class\n\nOur engineered capsids target multiple ocular tissues with differentiated enrichment profiles\n\nCapsida's Platform Enables Rapid Entry Into New Therapeutic Areas\n\n...\n\n### Summary\n\nBuilt a field-leading capsid engineering platform that enables rapid, at-scale capsid discovery\n\nIdentified > 5 breakthrough CNS capsids, each leveraging a distinct mechanism, expanding \nthe BBB-crossing playbook \nLead capsid drives three differentiated CNS programs into the clinic, with CAP-002 STXBP1- \nDEE having received FDA IND clearance \n\nIn-house GMP manufacturing ensures high-quality, scalable capsid production, accelerating development and enabling IND success\n\nExpanded into ophthalmology with potential best-in-class capsids; broad IP portfolio and platform capabilities position us to enter any therapeutic area\n\n---\n\nTitle: Science & Innovation - Capsida Biotherapeutics\nURL: https://capsida.com/science-innovation/\nPublished: 2022-08-08T00:00:00.000Z\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\nFor diseases of the eye, Capsida is directing its platform to engineer capsids for local intravitreal (IVT) and suprachoroidal (SCS) delivery.\n\n...\n\n### CAPSID ENGINEERING AND PRECLINICAL\n\nAt Capsida, the scale at which we have engineered capsids is unrivaled. Using our automated, high-throughput biological screening, our scientists assess large, diverse engineered capsid libraries for CNS and the eye in models relevant to humans to quickly identify optimal capsids that target tissues and cells in organs of interest.\n\nWe have developed engineered capsids for the brain that transduce >70% of neurons brainwide, generating a significantly increased therapeutic index. We have identified novel human blood-brain barrier receptors that bind our engineered capsids and are conserved between primates and humans. Our therapies can deliver a broad range of cargos including gene replacement, gene editing, gene silencing and vectorized antibodies, among others.\n\nCapsida’s engineered capsids for ocular diseases have improved RNA enrichment in the retina compared to clinical capsids while utilizing less invasive IVT and SCS dosing.\n\n---\n\nTitle: Capsida Biotherapeutics\nURL: https://capsida.com/wp-content/uploads/Capsida-Aug-2025-corp-deck.pdf\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: Julie Hakim\nHighlights:\n#### Next-generation Genetic Medicines Company\n\nUnlocking the full potential of gene therapy for all\n\nWholly-owned Pipeline External Validation\n\nStrategic partnerships\n\nContract manufacturing\n\n1st AbbVie opt-in ($40M) achieved\n\nFully-integrated Capabilities » Capsid engineering » Cargo optimization » Clinical development » In-house manufacturing » Protected by expansive IP portfolio\n\n>$300M funding to date, including $50M Series A\n\nCAP-002: STXBP1-DEE IND clearance ODD granted Fast Track granted\n\nCAP-004: Friedreich’s ataxia\n\nCAP-003: PD-GBA\n\n• IND clearance \n• Human POC in Q4 \n\nTwo clinical programs in 2025\n\nThird clinical program in 2026\n\n...\n\n#### Clinical Stage Wholly-owned Programs First human POC by end of 2025\n\nDisease / Target Preclinical IND-Enabling Phase 1/2 Key Catalysts\n\n| STXBP1 Developmental and Epileptic Encephalopathy (STXBP1-DEE) | | First-in-class CAP-002 | 2024 2025 2026 | Q4 Q2 Q3 Q1 | ODD received IND clearance received Fast-track designation received ‐ First patient dosed ‐ First efficacy data |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Parkinson’s disease associated with GBA mutations (PD-GBA) | | Best-in-class CAP-003 | 2025 2026 | Q2 Q3 Q4 Q3 | IND clearance received ‐ First patient dosed ‐ First biomarker data ‐ First efficacy data (1 yr) |\n| Friedreich’s ataxia (FA) Capsida is the first genetic medicines company with 2 FDA IND clearances for engineered IV-delivered | gene therapies that cross the blood-brain-barrier and detarget | Best-in-class CAP-004 | 2025 2026 | Q1 Q3 2H | ‐ IND-enabling studies ongoing ‐ Traditional & self-regulating cargo results ‐ IND filing liver |\n\n...\n\n#### CAP-003: PD-GBA\n\nParkinson’s disease associated with GBA mutations\n\nOpportunity\n\